.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-038-bound-goal-template-autocomplete-discovery.md:20:Make `/goal <string>` and `/goal queue <string>` template autocomplete safe and bounded so starting Pi from a broad directory such as `/Users/bryan` does not synchronously scan the entire home tree, freeze the TUI, spin fans, or trigger macOS folder permission prompts.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-038-bound-goal-template-autocomplete-discovery.md:24:The user reported a severe runtime failure: Pi was started in the home folder, which does not have a root `.pi-goals` directory, and `/goal <string>` autocomplete/search froze. The Mac then requested access to multiple home folders. This strongly suggests autocomplete was walking privacy-protected home-directory trees while looking for reusable goal templates.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-038-bound-goal-template-autocomplete-discovery.md:26:The current implementation confirms the likely root cause: autocomplete calls reusable-template discovery synchronously, and discovery recursively searches all descendants of `process.cwd()` for directories named `.pi-goals`.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-038-bound-goal-template-autocomplete-discovery.md:30:- `/goal` autocomplete stays responsive even when `process.cwd()` is a large directory with no templates.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-038-bound-goal-template-autocomplete-discovery.md:31:- Autocomplete/template discovery does not recursively traverse arbitrary home/workspace descendants.
